A||||6||GWMORGAN||Which Clutch?||||1||
Z||000000||GWMORGAN||05-24-2000||09:52 PM||||I have an 86GT with an Isuzu 5spd tranny. I'm about replace the clutch and would like to know which one I should use. Will the v6 clutch work with the Isuzu tranny, and if not, why?<BR>Thanx.||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||05-24-2000||11:58 PM||||Use the clutch for the Isuzu... TO bearing and all. In other words, when you order/ask for the clutch, don't even mention the V6.<P>Not sure why the V6 clutch will not work, but it won't... trust me! I found out the hard way. The car just wouldn't move.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||05-25-2000||02:16 AM||||Thanx SCCA....My friend (fellow fiero owner) and I will be replacing the clutch this week-end. Should take us about 8 hrs. tops.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cobra427||05-25-2000||10:00 PM||||GWMORGAN,<BR>you stated that you had an Isuzu trans in your 86 GT. This may help you identify which trans you have assuming that it has not been changed in the past.For 86 there was the:<BR>MT2 5 speed =Isuzu    85-88<BR>MG2 5 speed = Muncie  86-88<P>cobra||||reg||1
Z||000004||GWMORGAN||05-25-2000||10:18 PM||||Cobra...I originally had the Munchie 4spd. in my GT and had it replaced with the Isuzu 5spd. from an 87 4 cylinder.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sillhouette.com||05-25-2000||10:21 PM||||Your quite smart in keeping the five speed isuzu tranny.  Much better in precision and ease shifting than the monzie.   <BR>Now if your changing your clutch may I suggest perhaps a centerforce clutch.  It held me out for years with racing in solo courses. <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000006||GWMORGAN||05-26-2000||02:18 PM||||Sillhouette...My fiero piggy bank is depleted of funds and I can't afford a centerforce clutch (would've love to). For now I'll be using a "Brute Power" clutch, which, according to the guy at the parts store, is made by Borg Warner (or is it Wagner?) from scratch (not remanufactured).||||reg||1
